@host = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@email = juan.test@test.com
@password = password123

# Orden pensado para probar el flujo de auth de punta a punta.
# Los requests dependen del estado que dejan los anteriores (variables @name):
#   register -> login -> me -> refresh -> login2 -> logout
# Ejecútalos en orden. Se declara una segunda sesión (login2) para poder
# revocar de verdad en el logout y además probar su idempotencia.

### 1. Health  -> 200
GET {{host}}/health

### 2. Register  -> 201  (si repites, da 409; cambia @email)
# @name register
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Juan",
  "apellido": "Pérez",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3. Register con email repetido  -> 409 EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Juan",
  "apellido": "Pérez",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 4. Login  -> 200  (guarda accessToken y refreshToken)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 5. Login con password incorrecta  -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "password-incorrecta"
}

### 6. Me  -> 200  (perfil del usuario autenticado)
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 7. Me sin token  -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{host}}/auth/me

### 8. Me con token inválido  -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer token-de-mentira

### 9. Refresh  -> 200  (rota el par de tokens)
# @name refresh
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### 10. Refresh con el token VIEJO  -> 401 (reuso; además revoca la familia)
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### 11. Refresh sin token  -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR con errors[]
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 12. Login 2  -> 200  (segunda sesión, para revocar en el logout)
# @name login2
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 13. Logout  -> 200  (revoca el refresh token de login2)
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login2.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### 14. Logout repetido  -> 200 (idempotente, no falla aunque ya esté revocado)
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login2.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### 15. Refresh tras logout  -> 401 (token revocado server-side)
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login2.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### 16. 404
GET {{host}}/no-existe
